{
  "requirement": "Where subagents are unavailable, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to review each group themselves against the review prompt of {cite}`requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.review_prompt`, one group at a time, before presenting any group to the user.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has these testable obligations. The `habeas-requirements` skill must direct agents, where subagents are unavailable, to:\n- review each group themselves;\n- review it against the review prompt;\n- review one group at a time;\n- finish all of this before any group is presented to the user.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_reviews_groups_itself_without_subagents]` is marked `{test}` for the subject. It covers each obligation:\n- **Fallback wording.** It calls `step_of` with the exact sentence \"If you can't start subagents, review each group yourself against the prompt, one group at a time\". `step_of` panics if no workflow step of the bundled `habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` contains that sentence. `workflow_steps` collapses each step's indented continuation lines first, so the check works across the file's line wraps. I confirmed the sentence is in step 3 of `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`. That one phrase covers three obligations: the agent reviews the groups itself, it does so against the prompt, and it does so one group at a time.\n- **Ordering.** It asserts the fallback step's number is lower than the number of the step containing \"Present each group to the user\". That is step 4 in `SKILL.md`, so the fallback comes before any group is presented.\n\nA skill that dropped the fallback, dropped the one-at-a-time wording, or put the fallback after presentation would fail this test. The test does not separately assert that the prompt is the `references/review-prompt.md` one. The phrase \"against the prompt\" together with the step's earlier instruction to read that file carries this, and the content of the review prompt belongs to `requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.review_prompt`. That requirement is cited here, so I did not reassess it. No obligation is left untested, and there are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments to account for.",
  "references": "745a2eee305767915036fa4c6d7e81a0dae3d8dfb2fbb9f24b26e0da5c7070e8",
